name 'ai-and-algorithmic-decisions-postassessment-q3_2025'

question 'A restaurant\'s online order form has a "Place Order" button. When clicked, it checks that all required fields are filled out, shows a "Thank you!" message, and clears the cart for the next customer. What best describes what\'s happening in the code when the button is clicked?'

wrong 'The browser automatically saves the page and re-loads it without using any JavaScript.'
right 'An event handler detects the click and runs a set of programmed steps to finish the order.'
wrong 'A variable stores the thank-you message so users can\'t edit it.'
wrong 'The site\'s CSS file changes colors to show that an order is complete.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 2
